{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Until when for this evil congregation, etc.</b> These are the spies, and so they said in the Mishnah of Sanhedrin (108b). And His saying <b>et the murmurings of the children of Israel</b> refers to the rest of the congregation. And His saying <b>until when</b> intends to say that they were still frightening Israel to turn away from after HaShem, and therefore He called them an evil congregation, to say that it still stands in its wickedness. And His saying <b>whom they set against Me</b> means that besides their own wickedness, they further set Israel against Me." "<b>et the murmurings of the children of Israel, etc., I have heard.</b> It was necessary to inform that He heard, to say that He heard only the murmurings of the children of Israel and not the words of the wicked spies. And the construal of the verse is as follows: et the murmurings of the children of Israel, whom the spies set against Me, I have heard — meaning, the murmurings of the children of Israel, not the lodging of the spies, for the words of the spies themselves were abhorrent and He prevented them from reaching His ears."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Mishnah Sanhedrin 108b cited by page number in the Vilna edition; the abbreviation ק״ה resolved as 108."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:22.659719653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}